# UI test conventions

`baseURL` in `playwright.config.ts` stays `http://127.0.0.1:3200`. Do not change it to a non-loopback host. Do not point `DATABASE_URL` at anything but the throwaway database on `127.0.0.1:55433`, container `leave-e2e-db`.

Do not delete `tests/e2e/support/global-setup.ts`. Do not remove `globalSetup` from `playwright.config.ts`. Do not edit `app/` to make a test pass.

One `test.describe` per feature area. The title starts with the scenario id. Ids are unique across `tests/e2e/specs`. A new file in an existing area continues that area's numbering.

Page flows (`submitLeave`, `decide`, `openApprovals`) live in `tests/e2e/support/ui.ts`. Auth, assertions, and dates live in `app.ts`. Database readers live in `records.ts`. Policy math lives in `rules.ts`. Employee creation lives in `provision.ts`. Import `test` and `expect` from `fixtures.ts`.

`yearPlan().weekdays[0]` is today when today is a weekday. A case that needs a future date uses `futureWeekday(plan)`.

Filter every `getByRole("alert")` on the sentence. The Pending chip on HR approvals filters by request status only. A pending cancellation is decided from the All view. `decide()` is for the request, not the cancellation.

```ts
import { test, expect } from "../support/fixtures";
import { expectSuccess } from "../support/app";
import { leaveRequest, sqlString } from "../support/records";
import { leaveSummary, yearPlan } from "../support/rules";
import { requestRow, submitLeave } from "../support/ui";

test.describe("Leave requests", () => {
  test("LEAVE-POS-01 a full weekday stays pending", async ({
    freshEmployee,
    db,
    uniqueTag,
  }) => {
    const date = yearPlan().weekdays[0];
    const note = `LEAVE-POS-01 ${uniqueTag}`;
    const page = await freshEmployee.signedInPage();

    await test.step("Submit one full weekday", async () => {
      await submitLeave(page, {
        start: date,
        end: date,
        note,
        summary: leaveSummary(1, 8),
      });
      await expectSuccess(page, "Leave request saved for HR review.");
      await expect(requestRow(page, note)).toContainText("Pending");
    });

    expect(await leaveRequest(db, note)).toMatchObject({
      status: "Pending",
      reviewerId: "",
      email: freshEmployee.email,
    });
    expect(
      await db.query(
        `SELECT count(*)::text FROM requests WHERE note = ${sqlString(note)}`,
      ),
    ).toEqual([["1"]]);
  });
});
```

Isolate rows with `freshEmployee` or `uniqueTag`. Assert the visible outcome and the database row. A negative asserts that nothing was written for that actor. Wrap interpolated SQL with `sqlString`. The SQL command is `node tests/e2e/support/environment.mjs sql "<query>"`.

A confirmed app bug stays a correct-behavior test. Do not loosen the assertion so the wrong behavior passes.

```ts
test.info().annotations.push({
  type: "app-bug",
  description: "Weekend-only leave is saved. It must be refused.",
});
test.fail();
```
